PATCH 220: reconstruct FUN_0000_8791 (a display-object per-type INIT method dispatched by d755's
near-vector, the 7bcf sibling) -- the same DGROUP-near-offset base-loss class.  Asm-verified vs
re_out/fist_dat_image.bin 0x8791-0x87ca.

Reached as d755's display-object walk advances to the next roster object (di=0xc157, an enemy roster
slot).  param_1 = di; Ghidra treated it as a HOST pointer -> SIGSEGV.  DS=DGROUP=0x1c00, every [di+N]
is a DS-relative byte/word field.  Reconstructed with the explicit g_mem+0x1c000 base + the asm
byte/word widths (0x6dae==2 branch + seg-0x2c9f template copy to DGROUP:di+0xbc via 1e27).

Cascade-only => BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL for the 19 verify flows (reached ONLY via the mission display-setup
walk d755).  Default boot rc=0, mainmenu unchanged.  Sources pristine; fist.c via build/.
